    "explanation": "Both of you: this is trip TRP-00111, Blk 511 Woodlands Drive 14 to Fusionopolis, one-north, on 3 August 2026. The arithmetic of the trip is not in dispute. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00111) ran 29.98 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 24.0 km (EV-TRIP-00111) — an excess of 5.98 km, 24.92% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a route deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 requires the trace figure to be used, not the trip record's rounded 30.0 km copy. The trace is unimpaired: 229 fixes at 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, no gaps, so POL-RD-07 does not fire.\n\nThe driver's explanation is an external traffic cause, so under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the traffic advisory on file and nothing else. EV-ADVIS-00111-01 is an LTA DataMall record of a lorry fire closing the PIE towards Tuas after the Clementi Rd exit, valid 07:10–09:30, diversion via Upper Bukit Timah Rd. All three POL-RD-03 limbs are met: the advisory names a corridor the optimal route (BKE southbound then PIE westbound) uses; its window brackets the whole trace (07:47:40–08:25:40, 41.5 minutes of overlap); and the vehicle left the optimal corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment and rejoined after — which the driver announced in the in-app chat at 07:54:20 (EV-CHAT-00111), which both parties' own accounts describe, and which the trace's 29.98 km matches against the advisory's 29.2 km lawful alternative. The rider's point that this limb rests only on an assessor's narrative note does not survive: the contemporaneous chat message and both parties' descriptions place the exit and rejoin on the record.\n\nThe exoneration is capped. Justified excess = min(5.98 km measured, 1.30 × (29.2 − 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km) = 5.98 km. The whole excess is inside the cap, so the closure-adjusted optimal is 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km, with duration 30.0 × (29.98 / 24.0) = 37.5 minutes. Recomputing the fare under POL-RD-02 against that adjusted route, at the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00111): (3.80 + 0.75 × 29.98 + 0.28 × 37.5) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 37.585. The amount charged was SGD 37.74. The difference is SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so no refund issues and the present state stands.\n\nThe rider's figure of SGD 6.75 is computed against the booked optimal (recomputed fare SGD 31.00). That is the wrong baseline once POL-RD-03 applies: where POL-RD-03 excuses the excess, POL-RD-02 runs against the closure-adjusted optimal, not the booked one. The rider's assertion that there was no closure is outweighed by the LTA advisory, and the driver's traffic cause therefore does not fall away.\n\nNo other money moves. Tolls/ERP are 0.00 with no gantry crossed on either route, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to settle and there is no billing-integrity referral. No driver compensation arises: the billed 30.0 km is not less than the trace's 29.98 km, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall under POL-RD-04. No repeat-deviation referral: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 588 completed trips in 90 days and no material deviation remains after the adjustment, so POL-RD-06 does not engage; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags field is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. Every artifact relied on carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies and confidence sits at the top of the range. The monetary effect is nil and therefore below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold. This ruling is provisional; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
